{{also|gurkha}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Gorkha|Ghurkha|Ghoorka|Goorka|Goorkha}} {{qual|some forms are archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ne|गोर्खा|t=inhabitant of Gorkha}}, from {{m|ne|गोरखा}}/{{m|ne|गोर्खा|t={{w|Gorkha District}}}}, from {{der|en|sa|गोरक्ष|t=cowherd}} an epithet of the patron deity {{w|Gorakhnath}}, from {{com|sa|गो|रक्ष्|t1=cow|t2=protect|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)kə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|Gurkha}}

# A member of the dominant [[ethnic]] [[group]] in [[Nepal]], with a Himalayan diaspora.
# A member of this people recruited to serve in their own elite units in the [[British]] and [[Indian]] [[army|armies]].

====Usage notes====
* While ''Gurkha'' has been the popular spelling worldwide, inside Nepal, the correct spelling is considered to be ''Gorkha''.

